{"title":"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(easiest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (easiest)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the expansion of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e42212799afc8b50d066ff0471255746cf718dec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(1 + x + x^2 + \\cdots + x^{27}\\right)\\left(1 + x + x^2 + \\cdots + x^{14}\\right)^2,\\]\" width=\"391\" height=\"25\" />\nwhat is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Coefficient\" title=\"Coefficient\">coefficient</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf328af9579c7a405a8692453b578ef97f4fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/1/631516591f329b285cb11246db12736b23482a9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 195\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 196\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 224\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 378\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 405$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"432\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28easiest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(easiest)\">Solution 1 (easiest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (easiest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7bb3c9caa5fb9981ea77a0fe1b572753d3a2648.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\left(1 + x + x^2 + \\cdots + x^{14}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"228\" height=\"23\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73691029363b78ad667e253dbb3893ba29b9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\left(1 + x + x^2 + \\cdots + x^{27}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"224\" height=\"22\" />. We are expanding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20b1be742326c6fdbad68d203697d300f3f2d6ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\cdot A \\cdot B$\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> terms in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/8/a5862a79756d47017889ee5f1506601128979a53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15^2 = 225$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> ways to choose one term from each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. The product of the selected terms is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c72f3acf1f7744cfe76edaf47e45d62432cf28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^n$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inclusive. For each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df3f9bd7ea38f7336f5a64109d4053d775858f28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />, there is one and only one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/279128acca1e129f7c0c2a1d685640302a474910.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28 - n}$\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. For example, if I choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> , then there is exactly one power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> that I can choose; in this case, it would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d16033c998eff303abe418fc264b4dcb59192418.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{24}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />. Since there is only one way to choose one term from each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to get a product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/eda9cb06647e9f40c563a46b475f4ae23decad20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^0$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/f/d0f92b803e35d284996d08177468def3e5ac8805.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$225 - 1 = 224$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"110\" height=\"13\" /> ways to choose one term from each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and one term from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to get a product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf328af9579c7a405a8692453b578ef97f4fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />. Thus the coefficient of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf328af9579c7a405a8692453b578ef97f4fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c4cb3b0041ed9836f130b8440f696432d084a17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$224 \\Rightarrow \\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe8623d95d4296c02e03e5599a1ac497e3176f62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = \\left(1 + x + x^2 + \\cdots + x^{14}\\right)^2 = a_0 + a_1x + a_2x^2 + \\cdots + a_{28}x^{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"519\" height=\"25\" />. Then the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf328af9579c7a405a8692453b578ef97f4fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> term from the product in question <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e14a80b1826681ae2767f614ffa57f80ff0e4816.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(1 + x + x^2 + \\cdots + x^{27}\\right)(a_0 + a_1x + a_2x^2 + \\cdots + a_{28}x^{28})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"441\" height=\"22\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf3cb8c8c2327f10363073a9d73aa0498493f08b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1a_{28}x^{28} + xa_{27}x^{27} + x^2a_{26}x^{26} + \\cdots + x^{27}a_1x = \\left(a_1 + a_2 + \\cdots a_{28}\\right)x^{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"534\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>So we are trying to find the sum of the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> minus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5c7c921b3334f6ecf58c241eeea42acf0ce71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />. Since the constant term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5c7c921b3334f6ecf58c241eeea42acf0ce71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> (when expanded) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the sum of the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/7/797a20647c81f3259c5069556cab51c94bf4b752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />, we find the answer to be\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/d/6dd659a5f3bda304a4fa04c0178dffa85711a13d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(1) - a_0 = \\left(1 + 1 + 1^2 + \\cdots 1^{14}\\right)^2 - 1 = 15^2 - 1 = 224 \\Rightarrow \\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"492\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We expand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/0/940b6ade48b6649f36626cf064b026e2cb57bb62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 + x + x^2 + x^3 + \\cdots + x^{14})^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"232\" height=\"19\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a94bebe300dfaa9e3adc918e2e5c71cc861f808c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 + x + x^2 + x^3 + \\cdots + x^{14}) * (1 + x + x^2 + x^3 + \\cdots + x^{14})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"471\" height=\"21\" /> and use FOIL to multiply. It expands out to:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/0/eb0cacfa5bf738e58f5e64b2ece6427207c09cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + x + x^2 + x^3 + x^4 + \\cdots + x^{14} +$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"265\" height=\"16\" />  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/4346ceea754a592873a374ef2f05ca838a8b395a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\qquad x + x^2 + x^3 + x^4 + \\cdots + x^{14} + x^{15} +$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"314\" height=\"16\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/8/bd80303ada7ce3fcef76fe13b232fad6a94c8465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\qquad \\qquad x^2 + x^3 + x^4 + \\cdots + x^{14} + x^{15} + x^{16} + \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"389\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>It becomes apparent that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9fffd1dcbbf8894692e043faa57e2c20baf71ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 + x + x^2 + x^3 + \\cdots + x^{14})^2 = 1 + 2x + 3x^2 + 4x^3 + \\cdots + 15x^{14} + 14x^{15} + 13x^{16} + \\cdots + x^{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"737\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Now we have to find the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf328af9579c7a405a8692453b578ef97f4fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> in the product: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec9d9b9144df4c21701c687d7ebe6ad12fc72b41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 + 2x + 3x^2 + 4x^3 + \\cdots + 15x^{14} + 14x^{15} + 13x^{16} + \\cdots + x^{28}) \\cdot (1 + x + x^2 + x^3 + \\cdots + x^{27})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"729\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>We quickly see that the we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf328af9579c7a405a8692453b578ef97f4fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> terms from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/e/53e4fe9f5da2c82cc8399a70df2d62ce18a840a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{27} \\cdot 2x$\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19c40090ed201b3f26ef58bd7f949eaf9b6abf4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{26} \\cdot 3x^2$\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9ceaee3944ab19fb84658d17afc8679cd48e8d8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{25} \\cdot 4x^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />, ... <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/e/53e9b9d5902a4752dec38d421dd3f99e127cb7e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15x^{14} \\cdot x^{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />, ... <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd90db370b796a075f505b09a3f3563720de71f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28} \\cdot 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />. The coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf328af9579c7a405a8692453b578ef97f4fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> is just the sum of the coefficients of all these terms. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01d587572baeba9ded4c0b40cbd4f71af399c98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + \\cdots + 15 + 14 + 13 + \\cdots + 4 + 3 + 2 = 224$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"456\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rewrite the product as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e00a273695826b0aac1d1cf7306d0c14c6e0f016.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(x^{28} - 1)(x^{15} - 1)(x^{15} - 1)}{(x - 1)^3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"212\" height=\"43\" />. It is known that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/decfea45907427e1f67cbc5124a30764644b73fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{(1 - x)^n} = \\binom{n - 1}{n - 1} + \\binom{n}{n - 1}x + \\binom{n + 1}{n - 1}x^2 + \\binom{n + 2}{n - 1}x^3 + \\cdots + \\binom{n - 1 + k}{n - 1}x^k + \\cdots .\\]\" width=\"676\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Thus, our product becomes\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/e/18e59a7da67942850b7f55d0ae9fcee9cd482df4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-\\left( x^{28} - 1 \\right) \\left( x^{15} - 1 \\right) \\left( x^{15} - 1 \\right) \\left( \\binom{2}{2} + \\binom{3}{2}x + \\binom{4}{2}x^2 + \\cdots \\right).\\]\" width=\"506\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/9173b85d888cb0ad9d25887549b6e685ff6b083b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= -\\left( x^{28} - 1 \\right) \\left( x^{15} - 1 \\right) \\left( x^{15} - 1 \\right) \\left( 1 + 3x + 6x^2 + \\cdots \\right).\\]\" width=\"430\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>We determine the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf328af9579c7a405a8692453b578ef97f4fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> coefficient by doing casework on the first three terms in our product. We can obtain an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf328af9579c7a405a8692453b578ef97f4fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> term by choosing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf328af9579c7a405a8692453b578ef97f4fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> in the first term, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> in the second and third terms, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the fourth term. We can get two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf328af9579c7a405a8692453b578ef97f4fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> terms by choosing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/2/7c21997f17d38fe03ddecab51731d70dcb9b8831.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{15}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> in either the second or third term, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> in the first term, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> in the second or third term from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/2/7c21997f17d38fe03ddecab51731d70dcb9b8831.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{15}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> has not been chosen, and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/8/56861175455054ba851b22f83e012a0f4e8f8fc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{15}{2}x^{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"69\" height=\"53\" /> in the fourth term. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79a855e2691a404011938397681d4d2f09d9af77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{15}{2} * 2 = 210$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"123\" height=\"53\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf328af9579c7a405a8692453b578ef97f4fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> terms this way. (We multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/2/7c21997f17d38fe03ddecab51731d70dcb9b8831.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{15}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> term could have been chosen from the second term or the third term). Lastly, we can get an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf328af9579c7a405a8692453b578ef97f4fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> term by choosing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> in the first three terms and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/c/c6caff7d623507577cbb7c3cbf51b4891487abfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{30}{2}x^{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"69\" height=\"53\" /> from the fourth term. We have a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c911a1c743a015f72cb03030c9b4496b5ff72121.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 210 - 435 = -224$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"173\" height=\"14\" /> for the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cf328af9579c7a405a8692453b578ef97f4fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{28}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> coefficient, but we recall that we have a negative sign in front of our product, so we obtain an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f99d000f0d6d79349dc67b2513f1baf8db3b4da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$224 \\Rightarrow \\boxed{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"95\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the Stars and Bars Formula to create an equation<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbfc8b515b1ed5594ee0be7ddc372699e4d2184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />, with restrictions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/e/efe10c84c6c0343fb246682d923772a0f4e64443.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt;= 27, b&lt;=14, and c&lt;= 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"243\" height=\"18\" />. We also note that any variable can have a power of 0. \nUsing the formula (n + k - 1 choose k -1), we find that the total possibilities of getting an exponent of 27 is...\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0be9bb4eae1966ab6fde88c1cc2cdd85dc9345ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(28 + 2 choose 2) - [(2 choose 2) + (28 - 15 + 2 choose 2) + (28 - 15 + 2 choose 2)].$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"627\" height=\"20\" />\nWe stop since it is impossible for both variables to exceed the limit.\nTherefore, simplifying out equation we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc715052b011aa5ce58fc37bf0d3a0d4a3d35879.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(30 choose 2) - [1 + 2(15 choose 2)] = 435 - 211 = 224$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"416\" height=\"20\" />, correcponding to choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />!\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A\">2008 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2008 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017215015\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.071 seconds\nPrepr